# Patch:        010-raw-data-bounds
# Phase:        pre
# Target:       binary-pcs/src/boolean.rs, binary-pcs/src/boolean_trace.rs, binary-pcs/src/whir/boolean.rs, binary-pcs/src/whir/shape.rs
# Hunks:        12
# Class:        bound
# Gap:          docs/extractor-issues.md 10 (charon#1266): baby-bear's pre 020
#               drops `Field`'s `RawDataSerializable` supertrait under the
#               cfg, and binary-field's pre 010 then bounds the blanket
#               `BitCoordinates` impl on it. Without this patch rustc
#               nightly-2026-09-17 panics on p3-binary-pcs under the cfg
#               ("escaping bound vars"), while it reports the unmet bound on
#               a serde derive over the bit ring switch's claims proof.
# Cost:         none: each added bound is implied by `TowerLevel: Field` in a
#               normal build.
# Upstreamable: no: the bounds are redundant upstream. Dropping baby-bear's
#               pre 020 makes them unnecessary.
# Drop when:    baby-bear's pre 020 is dropped.
# Test:         test p3-binary-pcs --test whir_boolean; test p3-binary-pcs --test boolean
# Mutation:     the WHIR Boolean backend also asks its field to be an
#               iterator, which `TowerLevel` does not imply, so the test's
#               backend no longer compiles.
#
# The Boolean backends store the bit ring switch's claims proof, whose serde impls need a tower level's bytes.
#
# Under the cfg `TowerLevel` no longer implies them.
#
# rustc then fails to prove the derived impl's bound, and panics while it reports the failure.
#
# Stating the bound removes the panic, and 12 more bounds on the way satisfy every use:
#
# - the two serde bounds of the binary PCS's Boolean proof;
# - the Boolean backends of the binary PCS and of WHIR, and the trace commitment over them;
# - the WHIR proof shape of the bit readings.
#
# Every one of the 13 is needed: removing any one fails the cfg build.
#
# In a normal build `TowerLevel: Field` implies each bound, so nothing changes there.
#
